# The loose intermediates and the extraction bench's two products: kief, filtered kief, bubble hash,
# rosin and the moon rock.
#
# Redrawn 2026-09-14 against vanilla's own textures. Generated art, not Warlon Mhite's hand.
#
# ## Forms first: every member is told apart by silhouette before colour
#
#   item/hashish, item/filtered_hashish   an oblique slab      pressed          (hashish.mctex)
#   item/charas                           a rolled lump        hand-rolled      (charas.mctex)
#   item/kief, item/filtered_kief         a powder heap        sifted, loose
#   item/bubble_hash                      a pile of crumbs     washed and dried
#   item/rosin                            an amber sheet      squeezed out hot
#   item/moon_rock                        the bud, crusted     a bud, coated
#
# ## Kief and filtered kief: a settled heap, not vanilla's triangle
#
# A first pass borrowed the cone vanilla gives sugar and redstone, and Warlon Mhite called it what it
# was: mid. Kief is sifted dust, and dust settles: so this is a rounded dome that has slumped and
# spilled to one side, grained at nearly every pixel (a granular material is the one place dense
# variation is texture rather than noise), with trichome sparkle on the lit side and a few loose
# grains lying about the base -- which is how vanilla's glowstone dust and blaze powder break their
# heaps up too. Faintly olive, because trichome dust is greenish, which also keeps it off sugar and
# sand. Filtered kief is the same heap, blonder and warmer: one more pass, less leaf. Not stronger.

# ## Bubble hash: crumbs, not powder
#
# Ice-water hash dries as crumbly clumps, not dust, so it is three nuggets and two crumbs, drawn back
# to front with their own rims so the seams between them show. Warm pale tan with a grain in it --
# a first draft in cool grey read as gravel.
#
# ## Rosin: the amber sheet, and nothing under it
#
# Rosin comes off the press as a thin amber sheet. An earlier pass laid it on parchment; the paper
# made it read as a fried egg and, once the amber covered it, as a roast. So it is the sheet alone:
# an irregular flattened pool with a drip lobe, a darker rim, one pixel of front edge for its
# thickness, a lighter middle where it is thinnest, and one glassy streak up-left. The only glossy
# member besides charas.

# ## The moon rock: the mod's own bud, dipped and rolled
#
# A moon rock IS a bud -- dipped in rosin and rolled in kief -- so its silhouette is not drawn, it is
# taken: item/indica_buds' exact outline and its inner bract lines (both buds share them), which
# Warlon Mhite asked for after two invented nugs read as a potato and a sponge. The bud's own tones
# are mapped onto a golden kief ramp, the bract lines become the crevices of the coat, and sparkle
# goes on the lit side.
#
# Two layers, exactly as a packed device is. Layer 0 is that crust, the same for every strain.
# Layer 1 sits exactly on the bud's dark and mid strain pixels -- where the coat is thinnest in the
# recesses; with only the darkest, an indica and a sativa rock looked alike in a hotbar slot -- flat mid-grey and tinted at render time by StrainTintSource, so the strain shows
# through the kief the way a real moon rock's bud does. Every tinted layer in this mod is flat,
# because a shaded layer multiplied by a tint comes out muddy; and the mask must never sit on the
# rim, because layer 1 draws over it. (The mask's linter findings are a mask's, not the item's.)

@palette kief
. = none
1 = 3D3316      rim, and the shadow under the heap
2 = 5B4E24
3 = 7D6E33
4 = 9E8D48      the body
5 = BAA85E
6 = D3C27C      grains catching the light
7 = ECDFA8      trichome sparkle; scattered, never a band
8 = FFF4C8      its brightest glints

@palette filtered_kief
. = none
1 = 5A4222
2 = 7E612F
3 = A2803F
4 = C09B53
5 = D6B46F
6 = EACD94
7 = FAE8C0
8 = FFF8E4

